  "id": "returns-receiving",
  "title": "Returns Receiving",
  "summary": "A lighting shop gets returns in separate boxes. Keep the desk's approved quantities and the warehouse's counts in agreement.",
  "className": "ReturnsDesk",
  "starter": "class ReturnsDesk:\n    def __init__(self):\n        pass\n\n    def record_sale(self, order, sku, quantity, unit_cents):\n        pass\n\n    def request_return(self, claim, order, sku, quantity):\n        pass\n\n    def authorize_return(self, claim, quantity):\n        pass\n\n    def return_status(self, claim):\n        pass\n",
  "levels": [
    {
      "title": "Approve a return",
      "requirements": "The lighting shop has an order for three wall lamps. The customer asks to send all three back. The desk approves two. Keep the original request and the approval separate.\n\nrecord_sale(order, sku, quantity, unit_cents) records a fulfilled line. An order can have several lines. A line is identified by its order and SKU together. Both numbers must be positive integers. If the line already exists, keep the original quantity and price and return False. Return True after recording a new line.\n\nrequest_return(claim, order, sku, quantity) opens a request for one line. The sale line must exist and the claim ID must be new across the shop. The quantity must be from 1 through the number sold on that line. Pending requests can overlap. Return True if you record the request, or False if any check fails.\n\nauthorize_return(claim, quantity) approves an unapproved request once. The quantity must be from 1 through the number requested. The sum of approved quantities for the same sale line, including the new approval, cannot exceed the number sold. Return True on approval and False on failure. A failed approval leaves the request pending so staff can try a smaller quantity.\n\nreturn_status(claim) returns a list [requested, authorized]. Use 0 as the authorized count until approval. Return None for an unknown claim.\n\nA new desk has no sales or claims. Any failed write leaves the desk unchanged. All IDs and SKUs are nonempty, case-sensitive strings. The tests pass integers for quantities and amounts.",
      "visible": [
        {
          "id": "Customer asks for three, desk approves two",
          "kind": "requirements",
          "steps": [
