    {
      "title": "Count and inspect the boxes",
      "requirements": "A customer ships two boxes for one claim. A clerk scans each box at arrival. Staff can inspect its contents in smaller batches later.\n\nreceive_parcel(parcel, claim, quantity) records a box for an approved claim. The parcel ID must be new across the shop. The quantity must be positive. All parcels for the claim together can contain at most the approved quantity. Return True after recording the box, or False on failure. A parcel ID from a failed scan is still available.\n\ninspect_units(parcel, sellable, damaged) adds inspection counts to a known parcel. Both counts must be zero or greater, and their sum must be positive. The sum cannot exceed the number of units in that parcel that staff have yet to inspect. Return True and add both counts when the checks pass. Return False on failure.\n\nparcel_status(parcel) returns a list [received, sellable, damaged] for that parcel, or None if the parcel is unknown. Both inspection counts start at zero. Receiving and inspection leave the original request and approval counts unchanged.",
      "visible": [
        {
