    {
      "title": "Put units back on the shelf",
      "requirements": "Staff can send a sealed lamp back to the shop and keep a damaged one off the shelf. This shop refunds both after inspection. Stock and refund credit must track different counts.\n\nrestock(parcel, location, quantity) adds a positive number of sellable units from a known parcel to one location. The quantity cannot exceed that parcel's sellable units that staff have not already restocked at any location. Inspection alone does not add stock. Return True after restocking, or False on failure. Locations are nonempty, case-sensitive strings. You do not need to register them.\n\nstock_added(sku, location) returns the total units restocked for that SKU at that location across all returns. Return 0 when none have been restocked there. This count includes only stock added from returns.\n\nrefund_due(claim) returns the unpaid credit in whole cents. Each inspected unit, sellable or damaged, contributes the original unit price from the claim's sale line. Uninspected units contribute nothing. Restocking has no effect on the credit. Return 0 for a known claim with no credit and None for an unknown claim.",
